@@ -39,3 +39,18 @@ The first native draft exposed fixture artifacts: direct menu opening left the c
 ## Scope
 
 Production changes are in `inertial_carousel.gd`, `touch_scroll_container.gd`, `commerce_panel.gd`, `premium_hud.gd` and `companion_interface.gd`. The named `premium-ui-motion` suite is registered separately from core release checks. No commit or publish was performed by this critic.
+
+## Follow-up: context action at world boundaries
+
+The independent D2 front review found a real remaining obstruction in `evidence/d2-workplaces-final/mossMine_forge.png`: the FORGE action covered nearly the entire hero at the machine's actual interaction front. The first overview review had not exercised this pose.
+
+The context action now occupies the same bottom row as the bag and mining action, immediately to the bag's left. Its mobile area remains 206×104 logical pixels, with unchanged authored icon, font and caption. The middle-right gameplay region is open. Status text uses the available left portion of the bottom row whenever it would overlap the action, with up to two wrapped lines. It remains transparent to movement input.
+
+Verification after this repair:
+
+- Six iPhone layout sizes pass the existing 44 CSS-pixel target requirements plus new assertions for bottom-row alignment, a free movement half and status/action separation.
+- The 1.0 UI suite again passes **305 checks** and touch passes **123 checks**. Results: `qa-results/premium-ui-motion/action-row/results.json`.
+- The unchanged production D2 collision/camera fixture captured **16 actual station and arrival poses over all four biomes, 72/72 checks**, with no reported Godot error. Evidence: `/workspace/scratch/bcf004da8655/evidence/context-action-row/`.
+- Visual inspection confirms the full hero and companion are clear in `mossMine_forge.png`, `mossMine_sell.png`, `moonMine_wayfarer.png` and the right-boundary `mossMine_arrival.png`. This is native source-runtime evidence, not physical iPhone validation.
+
+The rendered-runner error gate briefly had mixed tab/space indentation from a concurrent edit. Two indentation lines were repaired; its new runtime-error detection remains active.
